-----------------------------------------------------------------------
ADDING A TEST
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. Add a recipe to RECIPES in make_polygons.py, then
         python3 make_polygons.py <name>
  2. Copy a deck, point it at <name>.poly, set the orientation and
     the header lines:
         # polygon  : <name>.poly
         # expect   : valid | error
         # reason   : <text the ERROR must contain>     (error only)
         # warns    : <text a WARNING must contain>     (optional)
         # check    : [refined] <mesh file> <poly>[,<poly>...]
                                                        (optional)
         # min_angle: <deg>   smallest angle every refined mesh must
                              reach (optional; else only reported)
         # boundary_angle: <deg>  largest angle facing a boundary edge
                              in a refined mesh (90 for control volumes)
         # picture  : small | large   picture size on the page
     A deck with no expect line FAILS. With no "# check" line the deck
     must dump its mesh to out_<deck>.inp and is checked against its
     "# polygon". "# check" lines (one or more) name each mesh to check
     and its polygons instead; "refined" allows new vertices.
  3. Keep every name in the deck to 32 characters or fewer: LaGriT
     truncates longer tokens (the runner FAILs such a deck).

